ch Atlas is not blind, and give it the F1 treatment. The handling rule: a note is scanned on write, any section 3.1 field found is refused with invalid_input and the field name logged, never the value, and the note is stored only when clean. Close Q5 in the page with that answer, marked PROPOSED. HOST NAMES, decided 2798: the two pilot hosts are ChatGPT and Claude, and the founders ruled the spec may name them as pilot targets. Fill the two host name slots at lines 249 to 258. Leave the authorization-flow and consequential-action columns as explicitly unread placeholders exactly as they are, since those get filled from each host current documentation in W1; do not fill them from memory. INVITE GATE, decided 2799: add one sentence to the identity section stating that the gate is untouched for the pilot, the five testers are placed on the allowlist before they connect, no gated-connect experience is built, and public signup at connect waits for the gate to come down. VERIFY, real exit codes captured directly rather than read after a pipe: make check-prd-index, and confirm git diff touches only the page and the PR body. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash character in any added line, commit message or PR text; no AI tool or vendor name in commit or PR text; the host names ChatGPT and Claude are permitted inside the page only, as product substance. Push to the SAME branch so PR 2802 updates in place; do not open a new PR; do not merge. Add one comment to PR 2802 listing what changed per finding and naming the two decisions folded in. Omit any Co-Authored-By trailer. | docs/prd-assistant-channel-w0

